# ─── Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default-deny on env files, then allow the one template back.
#
# .env.local currently holds a Supabase service-role key (bypasses every RLS
# policy), a Postgres password, a Slack bot token, and the QuickBooks, Plaid and
# Stripe credentials. Any one of those in a commit is a credential rotation, and
# git history keeps it after the file is deleted.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Encryption keys, certificates, service-account files
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
service-account*.json

# ─── Dependencies and build output ──────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
.vercel/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated by `next dev` / `next build`; regenerated on demand.
next-env.d.ts

# ─── Test and tooling artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.eslintcache

# ─── Real financial data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bank statements and payroll exports must never reach a repository. The
# templates in samples/ are fabricated and ARE committed - keep real exports
# somewhere else, or drop them in a folder matching these patterns.
*-statement.csv
*-export-real.csv
private/
statements/

# ...but the fabricated templates are the point of samples/, and
# vn-bank-statement.csv matches the pattern above, so allow that folder back.
!samples/
!samples/**

# ─── Editors and operating systems ──────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ─── Scratch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tmp/
temp/
*.local.md

# ─── Deliberately NOT ignored ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# supabase/setup-all.sql  - generated from the migrations, but committed on
#                           purpose: it is what someone pastes into the Supabase
#                           SQL editor when they cannot run `npm run db:push`.
# samples/*.csv           - fabricated templates for checking column mapping.
# docs/                   - the decision log and outstanding-work list.
